  "title": "# The API controls EVERYTHING in the console (Brett, Nov 7) Rule: the API (control@1 / MCP / CLI / …",
  "asked": "# The API controls EVERYTHING in the console (Brett, Nov 7) Rule: the API (control@1 / MCP / CLI / voice) must be able to do anything Brett can do by hand in the console and every plugin. Today it can't (e.g. it can open a terminal tab but can't type in it). ## Step 1: terminal typing (do first) - control@1 action to open a Terminal tab on a chosen target (vps / console / a build) AND to type into it: text is typed visibly, character by character at a readable speed (setting, default ~30 chars/s), then Enter. Brett watches it run live. Return the output. - Also: send keys (Ctrl-C, arrows, Tab), read the tab's screen, close the tab. Writes go through the orchestrator's VPS policy (reads instant, writes veto) once orchestrator-vps-gate lands; until then use the existing policy. - Console screen id for the Terminal must be openable by name (\"terminal\" today returns not_found). ## Step 2: audit every UI, one at a time Walk the console screen by screen, plugin by plugin (use ui-registry + console.screens/dialogs/settings/actions). For EVERY switch, setting, configuration, button, menu item, context-menu entry, toolbar action, dialog, tab and behaviour: check the API can read and change/trigger it. Record a coverage table (element, where, API path, status) in the report and as a registry file. ## Step 3: fill every gap Expose each missing one through control@1 (generic: any registered action/setting/element addressable by id), with MCP/CLI names. Approve/reject/pick in UI Review too, and approvals in place. ## Step 4: lock it CI check: fails if any UI element/setting/action has no API path. Rule into RULES.md and the brief template. UI from assets, no hard-coded styling. Tests. Add to Shipped features. Progress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
